xnu 0369: inject the probe into ReportCrash

Measured 2026-11-18: on a boot whose UI is clean -- SpringBoard once, no crashes,
Photos alive -- ReportCrash faults `sig 11` 81 times in ten minutes with the same
pc in a system library and the faulting address in a hole between two of its own
mappings, and every crash produces the report it then cannot process. The kernel's
`CRASH` line has the pc, lr and frame chain but not the images they land in, and
that is the one thing the probe already prints at exec.

The hook also arms a SIGSEGV/SIGBUS handler for the probe targets, so the line
names the image and offset of the faulting pc instead of a bare address.

--- a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
@@ -5698,6 +5698,14 @@
 		 * throw hook; this one needs the same.
 		 */
 		"MobileSlideShow",
+		/*
+		 * Its own death, not the UI's: measured 2026-11-18, ReportCrash
+		 * faults sig 11 with the faulting address between two of its own
+		 * mappings, 81 times in ten minutes, and every crash feeds the next
+		 * report it cannot process. The ring has the pc and the frame
+		 * chain but not the images they land in.
+		 */
+		"ReportCrash",
 	};
 	size_t i;
 
